spans.s:
) that by giving as a gift with composed mind (samāhitaḥ) roots and fruits to the Brāhmaṇas under the constellation Mūla (mūle mūlaphalaṁ dattvā) one delights the manes, and gets the desired state after death (gatim iṣṭāṁ ca gacchati) 13. 63. 24;

(2) śrāddha: Yama told Śaśabindu (13. 89. 1) that by offering a kāmya śrāddha under the Mūla one becomes healthy (mūle tv ārogyam arccheta) 13. 89. 10.

